  "body": "## What changed\n\n`lab()` in the notify tests makes its temp folders inside `<manifest>/target` but never created that folder. It now creates it first. Test-only.\n\n## Why\n\nWith `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` outside the worktree, a fresh worktree has no `target` folder, so most notify tests fail with `NotFound`. Only `world_with()` in `exec_tests.rs` creates the folder, so the result depends on test order, and a failed run could pass on the next one.\n\n## How it was tested\n\nFrom a worktree with no `target` folder and `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` set elsewhere, `cargo test --locked --lib runtime::notify`:\n\n- Before: 8 passed, 42 failed.\n- After: 50 passed, 0 failed.\n\n`cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --locked --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo test --locked` pass.\n",
